course: dictionary
lesson: 4065
title: Gentleness in words and deeds
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: Gentleness means being kind, calm and careful, not rough or harsh. It can also mean softness or mildness, like a gentle breeze or a gentle slope. «She stroked the puppy with gentleness.» Here gentleness shows how she touched the puppy: carefully, without rushing or squeezing.
explain: Look at the words around gentleness to find its meaning. «The fruit of the Spirit is love, joy, peace, patience, kindness, goodness, faithfulness, gentleness and self-control.» Every word in this list is a good quality, so gentleness is one too. Kindness and patience sit close by as clues.
explain: Gentleness is needed with babies, pets and people who are upset. «Little sisters need gentleness, not a lecture.» Notice the word not: a lecture can feel harsh, and gentleness is the calm, kind opposite. To check your meaning, swap in «kindness and calm care» and see if the sentence still makes sense.
fact: Gentleness means being kind, calm and careful, not rough or harsh.
fact: Gentleness can also mean softness or mildness, as in «the gentleness of a breeze».
fact: «Gentleness and kindness» are often said together because they go well together.
fact: Christians list gentleness among the «fruit of the Spirit» in Paul's letter to the Galatians.
fact: The Bible (1 Peter 3:15) asks Christians to be ready to give a reason for their hope, «with gentleness and respect».
exercise: «She stroked the puppy with gentleness.» What does gentleness mean here? | *Being careful and kind, not rough | Being loud and fast | Being very tired | Being far away
exercise: «The gentleness of the breeze made the leaves sway.» Gentleness here means what? | Speed and noise | *Softness and mildness | Darkness and cold | Harshness and force
exercise: In the list «love, joy, peace, patience, kindness, goodness», which word is closest in meaning to gentleness? | *kindness | joy | peace | love
test: «Little sisters need gentleness, not a lecture.» Why does the writer add the word not? | Because sisters like lectures | Because a lecture is also gentle | Because gentleness is loud | *Because a lecture is harsh, and gentleness is the calm, kind opposite
test: A friend is upset and crying. Which action shows gentleness? | Shout until they stop crying | *Speak softly and listen calmly | Walk off without a word | Laugh at them to cheer them up
exam: Which sentence uses gentleness to mean softness or mildness? | «The noisy crowd ran past the gate.» | «He slammed the door hard.» | *«The gentleness of the spring sun warmed the garden.» | «She shouted at the whole team.»
